# Two users insert different words at the SAME position of the same sentence.
# Yjs never flags this: it keeps both insertions and orders them by clientID.
# The order below is therefore not a spec -- it is characterization of a
# deterministic tie-break (see the golden transcript) -- but "no conflict" and
# "both words survive" are asserted.

doc master
  para "The quick fox."

branch review from master

as alice on master  insert p1 after "quick" " brown"
as bob   on review  insert p1 after "quick" " red"

merge review -> master
expect merged true
expect conflicts 0
show master
